🚽 Test case: round-22 review finding #4 -- a `bussin` (return)
🚽 expression was recursively visited (so a nested native call inside it
🚽 still got its own signature checked), but never compared against the
🚽 enclosing function's declared (return_type, return_pointer_level) at
🚽 all. `yapping(...)` statically resolves to VAR_VOID; `terrible()`
🚽 declares `rizz` (int). Only ast.c's handle_return_statement(), at
🚽 actual call time, would previously have caught this. Now rejected
🚽 statically, via the same check_type_compatibility_ex() machinery
🚽 every other declared-type comparison in this file already uses.
rizz terrible() {
    bussin yapping("oops");
}

skibidi main {
    bussin 0;
}
